TEXT 232 40 Left 2 ;SET:\nx-axis: v(i)\ny-axis: v(psi)
TEXT 144 160 Left 2 ;0 till three times of phi\nFor higher resolution from 0 till PHIN\nset 1*PHIN
TEXT 40 192 Left 2 !.param N1=1000 lm=10 Area=0.4084\neH H 0 value={N1*v(i)/lm} tripdv=1 tripdt=1\neB B 0 value={v(phi)/Area}  tripdv=1 tripdt=1\nemuer muer 0 value={V(b)/V(h)/(4*pi/1e7)}  tripdv=1 tripdt=1\nerm rm 0 value={lm/(v(muer)*Area*4*pi/1e7 )} tripdv=1 tripdt=1\neL L 0 value={v(phi)*N1/v(i)}
TEXT 40 -24 Left 2 ;The magnetizing curve is constructed by Lm, N1 and Area\nThe phi/i curve constructs the max. current at different phi's \nand is independent of the geometrical data\nThe transformer model has NO geometrical data at all\nThis data is only important to construct the BH curve. \nTo do this change the values of the geometrical data to get\nthe desired curves
